<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aristobulus II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/49-bce">49 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aristobulus II was Hasmonean king and high priest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judaea</a> from 67 to 63 BCE, a younger son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-jannaeus">Alexander Jannaeus</a> and Salome Alexandra. His civil war with his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyrcanus-ii">Hyrcanus II</a> drew in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>, who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 63 BCE and led him captive to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. He later escaped and was poisoned by Pompeian partisans in 49 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aristobulus-ii.jpg" alt="Aristobulus II" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Reverdy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aristobulus_II_medal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
